      "info": {
        "contact": {
          "name": "API Documentation",
          "url": "https://github.com/l0v3m0n3y/IPSB"
        },
        "description": "The IPSB API allows you to perform IP address lookups for both IPv4 and IPv6 addresses. It provides detailed information such as location, ISP, and other related data for any given IP address.",
        "servers": [
          {
            "description": "IP.SB API Server",
            "url": "https://api.ip.sb"
          }
        ],
        "title": "IP Address Lookup API",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "tagline": "Look up IPv4/IPv6 addresses and resolve them to location, ASN, and ISP details",
        "homepage": "https://ip.sb/",
        "docs_url": "https://ip.sb/api/",
        "license_short": "Free public service; GeoIP data by MaxMind GeoLite (attribution required)",
        "license_md": "- Operated by SB Professional Services, LLC as a free public service\n- Includes GeoLite data created by MaxMind, available from [maxmind.com](https://www.maxmind.com) — attribution required when redistributing geolocation results\n- API source derives from the open-source [Telize](https://github.com/fcambus/telize) project\n- No published rate limits or terms; treat as best-effort and avoid abusive usage",
        "about_md": "IP.SB is a free REST API that returns the caller's public IP address and resolves any IPv4 or IPv6 address to geolocation and network metadata. It is operated by [SB Professional Services, LLC](https://ip.sb/) alongside related services such as DNS.SB.\n\nWhat you get from the API:\n\n- Plain-text or JSON echo of the visitor's IP (`/ip`, `/jsonip`)\n- Geolocation lookup for the visitor or any supplied IP (`/geoip`, `/geoip/{ip}`)\n- Fields returned by GeoIP include country code and name, region code and name, city, postal code, continent code, latitude, longitude, timezone, ASN, and ISP organization\n- Dual IPv4/IPv6 endpoint variants and JSONP callback support\n\nNo API key or authentication is required and CORS is enabled. Geolocation is powered by MaxMind GeoLite data, so accuracy is approximate — especially at the city level. Invalid input IPs return HTTP 400 with a JSON error message.",
        "entity_desc": {
          "ipn": "An IP address record carrying geolocation and network attributes (country, region, city, postal code, latitude/longitude, timezone, ASN, ISP); served from `/jsonip`, `/geoip`, and `/geoip/{ip}`."
        },
